 {"id": "OBSDB-001", "title": "Emit /metrics on the duckbrain HTTP daemon (MVP: up, health_status, health probe latency, embedder health, read counter)", "status": "complete", "priority": "P0", "complexity": 2, "lane": "monitoring", "created_at": "2026-11-03T21:30:00Z", "reasoning": "WHY: DuckBrain emits no scrapable metric at all - there is no /metrics route (src/cli/http.ts:573-576 registers only /health and /stats), no Prometheus client in package.json, and a live curl against 127.0.0.1:3000 returns 401 for /metrics (auth middleware at src/cli/http.ts:532 answers unknown paths) while the daemon is currently serving status=degraded. The read ledger already stores per-request rows with durations (.duckbrain-audit/reads.jsonl, src/http/readLedger.ts:70-80) but never exports them, and the dark-port watchdog deliberately discards the /health body (src/cli/health-check.ts:22), so nothing converts health or traffic into a time series. WHAT: add prom-client and mount an auth-exempt, rate-limit-exempt GET /metrics next to /health in createHttpServer that exposes duckbrain_http_up (gauge), duckbrain_health_status (gauge 2/1/0 for healthy/degraded/hung, reusing ALIVE_STATUSES + HUNG_EXIT_CODE semantics from src/cli/health-check.ts:27-31), duckbrain_health_probe_duration_seconds (histogram, label probe=embedding|keys|total), duckbrain_embedding_provider_healthy (gauge, label provider), duckbrain_reads_total (counter, labels route/method/status_class, fed from the existing read-ledger row writer so no new hot-path work), and duckbrain_build_info (gauge 1, labels version/node). Labels MUST use the normalized route template from src/http/readLedger.ts:243-280 - never a namespace, key, id, user, path or timestamp. Full catalogue and label rules: docs/observability-spec.md sections 3-4. Do not touch service behaviour beyond instrumentation; /health body unchanged. ACCEPTANCE: (1) curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:3000/metrics | head -1 returns a '# HELP duckbrain_http_up' line with no Authorization header; (2) for m in duckbrain_http_up duckbrain_health_status duckbrain_health_probe_duration_seconds duckbrain_embedding_provider_healthy duckbrain_reads_total duckbrain_build_info: curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:3000/metrics | grep -q \"^$m\" - all six pass; (3) PromQL on fleet-monitor after the duckbrain scrape job is added: 'duckbrain_health_status{job=\"duckbrain\"}' returns a sample whose value equals the mapping of curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:3000/health | jq -r .status (healthy=2, degraded=1); (4) PromQL 'increase(duckbrain_reads_total[5m]) > 0' returns a series after one authenticated GET /api/namespaces; (5) grep of the exposition shows no metric line containing a namespace name, memory key or ISO timestamp label.", "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "a530621c", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "GET /metrics landed: six MVP families from prom-client, mounted before the rate limiter and before auth, fed by the existing read ledger. CI green on 800fc4a6 (run 41742913579); suite 249/2075; tsc clean.", "foreman_note": "LANDED a530621c (feat) + 800fc4a6 (chore/lock). Independent verification on a scratch daemon from the LANDED tree (/home/kara/clock/verify-obsdb001-main.sh, port 28541): 9 of 10 checks PASS — AC1 unauthenticated first line is '# HELP duckbrain_http_up'; AC2 five families present immediately; AC3 no namespace/key/timestamp labels; AC4 reads_total 0 -> 2 after an authenticated read; AC5 /health degraded -> duckbrain_health_status 1. The one non-pass is recorded rather than papered over: duckbrain_reads_total has NO series before its first observation, because prom-client renders nothing for a labeled counter without children — so a scrape on a freshly booted, idle daemon shows five families. AC4 proves the counter works after a read, and the implementer's own tests encode the same semantics deliberately ('a counter with no observation genuinely has no series'). CONSEQUENCE for monitoring: liveness must alert on absent(duckbrain_http_up), never absent(duckbrain_reads_total) — OBSDB-007 pins that. Label discipline is enforced by construction: observeRead refuses any route whose segments are not a literal or a :placeholder, so /api/ns/tenant-acme never becomes a label. MOUNT ORDER: /metrics before rateLimit and before authMiddleware, matching /health's precedent — an unauthenticated scrape must work, and a scrape that 429s is useless; the health snapshot behind it is TTL-cached 30s with a 10s deadline, so scrapes cannot amplify embedding probes. NOT LIVE YET: the production daemon (PID 3856050, running code from before this merge) still answers /metrics with 401 — deployment is OBSDB-007, and restarting it is the owner's call. Also fixed during landing: the worktree declared prom-client in package.json + pnpm-lock.yaml but not in the tracked package-lock.json, which is what Dockerfile:8 and CI install from — scripts/ci/check-lockfile-sync.sh said LOCKDRIFT and its own test failed (the only red file in the 249). Regenerated (+39 lines, no version churn); gate prints LOCKDRIFT: OK. The main checkout also needed 'pnpm install --frozen-lockfile' for the same reason — done, so a restart will not crash on a missing module.", "detail": {"evidence": [{"run_id":"41742913579","ts":"2026-11-04T00:02:25.746974+00:00"}]}}
 {"id": "OBSDB-002", "title": "Emit per-route read latency histogram and rejected-request counter (rate-limit 429 / DNS-rebind 403 are structurally invisible today)", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "lane": "monitoring", "created_at": "2026-11-03T21:30:00Z", "reasoning": "WHY: the read ledger records dur_ms per request (src/http/readLedger.ts:78, written at :109-150) but the only aggregation drops it - aggregateReadRows returns counts and status tallies only (src/http/readLedger.ts:338-400), so 'how long does a recall take at p95' has no answer anywhere; and throttled/blocked requests are never recorded at all because rateLimitMiddleware runs at src/cli/http.ts:458, BEFORE the read-ledger middleware at src/cli/http.ts:530, so the 429 emitted at src/auth/ratelimit.ts:159 and the 403 at src/cli/http.ts:447-451 produce zero telemetry. WHAT: add duckbrain_read_duration_seconds (histogram, labels route/method, buckets 0.01..30s to cover the measured 3s+ semantic recall path) populated in the read-ledger middleware's res 'finish' hook, and duckbrain_reads_rejected_total (counter, label reason=rate_limit|dns_rebind) incremented where those responses are produced. Keep the JSONL ledger as the durable audit of record; the metrics must not replace it. Spec: docs/observability-spec.md sections 2 (blind spots 3-4) and 3.2. ACCEPTANCE: PromQL 'histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, route) (rate(duckbrain_read_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))' returns a non-NaN value for route=\"GET /api/memories\" after at least 5 semantic recalls; and 'increase(duckbrain_reads_rejected_total{reason=\"rate_limit\"}[5m]) > 0' returns a sample after a burst that trips the 429 path, while grep -c 'duckbrain_reads_rejected_total{reason=\"rate_limit\"}' on /metrics is >= 1.", "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "933b39d9", "worker_summary": "Read latency and refusals are now series: duckbrain_read_duration_seconds (route/method, 10ms-30s) observes the ledger's own dur_ms, and duckbrain_rejected_total{reason,route} counts the 429s and DNS-rebind 403s that both run upstream of every existing sink.", "foreman_note": "LANDED 933b39d9 on main (0 unpushed at landing). Independent verification, scratch daemon port 28601 with --rate-limit=5, /home/kara/clock/verify-obsdb002.sh: (AC1) three reads produced duckbrain_read_duration_seconds_count{route=\"GET /api/namespaces\"}=2 and {route=\"GET /api/memories\"}=1 with non-zero _sum (0.00707 / 0.00621 s) across 22 populated buckets; (AC2) twelve rapid requests produced 10 real 429s, counted exactly as {reason=\"rate_limit\",route=\"GET /api/namespaces\"} 10; (AC3) a wrong-Host request produced a real 403 counted as {reason=\"dns_rebind\"} 1 — this is the seam that proves the guard hooks fire while the caller is already throttled, since the rebind guard is mounted above the limiter; (AC4) zero series carried namespace/key/id/path/timestamp labels; (AC5) all six OBSDB-001 families still render unauthenticated. WORKER NOTE (honest): the dispatched subagent implemented the source (276 insertions across 4 files) and tsc was clean, but it ended without writing tests or committing. I wrote src/http/metrics-obsdb002.test.ts myself (9 tests) and committed; my first draft used durationMs instead of the real durMs field and two assertions assumed POST routes normalize — both were MY errors, caught because the tests failed: a refused write legitimately classifies as (unmatched) since the classifier is the read-ledger truth table. Rebased onto 121aa62c before landing; test-counts.json 251/2088 matches the added file and tests. Deferred to the rules file (fleet-monitoring bac71ee): the read-error-ratio alert counts only real status classes so the reads counter's zero sentinel cannot dilute the denominator.", "detail": {"evidence": [{"run_id":"local-933b39d9","ts":"2026-11-04T00:24:50.750315+00:00"}]}}
